      "body": "## Motivation\n\nFixes #42139.\n\n`HunyuanDetector._stream_args` escapes a partial string value by hand (`\\\\`, `\"`, `\\n`, `\\r`, `\\t` only), but the final delta is diffed against `json.dumps(self._completed_args)`. Any other control character (`\\x00`-`\\x1f`, e.g. `\\b`, `\\f`, `\\x1f`) is streamed raw, and the final delta then appends the rest of its `\\u00XX` escape, so the concatenated `arguments` are not valid JSON. The issue's repro on current main:\n\n```\ndetect_and_parse : {\"a\": \"\\^_\"}\nstreamed         : '{\"a\": \"\\x1fu001f\"}'    # json.loads: Invalid control character\n```\n\n## Modifications\n\n- Build the partial value with `json.dumps(safe_value, ensure_ascii=False)[:-1]`, the same encoder as the final arguments minus the closing quote. `json.dumps` escapes each character on its own, so the escaping of a prefix is a prefix of the final escaping, and the streamed deltas concatenate to exactly the one-shot arguments.\n- Regression case: a string argument containing `\\x00 \\b \\f \\x1f \" \\ \\n`, streamed character by character, must equal the `detect_and_parse` arguments and decode back to the original value.\n\nNote for #45258 (open, O(N) streaming rewrite of this detector): its new incremental path keeps the same hand-written escaping, so it needs the same change.\n\n## Accuracy Tests\n\nParser-only change; no model-forward or kernel code is touched.\n\nLocal CPU run, Python 3.12:\n\n- `test/registered/unit/function_call/test_hunyuan_detector.py`: 45 passed. The new case fails on main and passes with this change.\n- `test/registered/unit/function_call/` plus `test/registered/unit/entrypoints/openai/test_serving_{chat,responses,responses_stream}.py`: 866 passed, no new failures compared with main. The 18 cases that fail in my environment fail the same way on main; they need packages that only ship Linux/macOS wheels (`deepseek-recipe`, `tml-renderers`, `uvloop`).\n- isort, `ruff check` (pre-commit selection), `ruff format --check` and codespell are clean on the changed files.\n\n## Speed Tests and Profiling\n\nNot applicable: the per-delta work is one `json.dumps` call on the partial value instead of five `str.replace` calls.\n\n## Checklist\n\n- [x] Format your code according to the [Format code with pre-commit](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#format-code-with-pre-commit).\n- [x] Add unit tests according to the [Run and add unit tests](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#run-and-add-unit-tests).\n- [ ] Update documentation according to [Write documentations](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#write-documentations). Not applicable.\n- [ ] Provide accuracy and speed benchmark results according to [Test the accuracy](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#test-the-accuracy) and [Benchmark the speed](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#benchmark-the-speed). Not applicable to a parser-only change.\n- [x] Follow the SGLang code style [guidance](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#code-style-guidance).\n\n<!-- pr-states:start -->\n---\n### CI States\n\nLatest PR Test (Base): <!-- slot:pr-test:start -->:x: [Run #40144195503](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/40144195503)<!-- slot:pr-test:end -->\nLatest PR Test (Extra): <!-- slot:pr-test-extra:start -->:x: [Run #40144195506](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/40144195506)<!-- slot:pr-test-extra:end -->\nLatest PR Test (AMD ROCm 10): <!-- slot:pr-test-amd:start -->:x: [Run #40144195468](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/40144195468)<!-- slot:pr-test-amd:end -->\n<!-- pr-states:end -->",
